# Warren Warleader: "Whenever you attack, choose one — Create a 1/1 white Rabbit creature token that's tapped and attacking." Bot1
# casts it on turn 1 without offspring (no token copy) and attacks with it on turn 3: the first mode makes a Rabbit token that
# enters tapped and attacking, so Bot2 takes 4 + 1. The token was never declared as an attacker, so the ability does not trigger
# a second time for it (the ruling), and the Warleader itself stays 4/4 (the other mode was not chosen).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Warren Warleader
Plains x4
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Warren Warleader.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Warren Warleader > Bot2)
Bot1.Modes(Create a 1/1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Rabbit Token.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Rabbit Token.Power = 1
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 15
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Warren Warleader.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Warren Warleader.Toughness = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Rabbit Token.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Rabbit Token.Toughness = 1
